{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And the reason for the male and the beast is well-known, for it is an abominable thing and is not among the continuance of the species, for man and beast do not produce offspring. And Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] (Ibn Ezra on Leviticus 18:22) wrote: since we find \"Behold, I lay last night with my father\" (Genesis 19:34), behold <b>you shall not lie</b> is a warning both to the one who lies and to the one who is lain upon. But if according to his words, why was the woman not included in \"and with any beast you shall not give your lying-down,\" for women are included in the warnings throughout the entire Torah. Rather, the reason for \"I lay last night with my father\" is because they lay with him in order that seed might emerge from him, as is known that the seed may come from the movement, or from the entire body, just as foam forms at the mouths of horses in their running, or it may be generated in the tendons near there and gather there by virtue of the surrounding movement and emerge, and if they had not lain upon him, seed would not have emerged from him, for he was like a silent stone in his drunkenness."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:55:31.509051767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}